[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\coordinate (A) at (0,3.464);
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,left] {$3\sqrt{3}$};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,below] {$3$};
\draw (C)--(A) node[midway,above right] {$6$};
\coordinate (ra1) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (ra2) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(C)$);
\draw (ra1)--($(ra1)+(ra2)-(B)$)--(ra2);
\pic[draw,"$60^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.62cm,angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle=A--C--B};
\pic[draw,"$30^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.5cm,angle eccentricity=1.7] {angle=B--A--C};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
This is a scaled $30^{\circ}$–$60^{\circ}$–$90^{\circ}$ triangle. From it, what is the exact value of $\cos60^{\circ}$?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\coordinate (A) at (0,3);
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (3,0);
\draw (A)--(B);
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,below] {$x$};
\draw (C)--(A) node[midway,above right] {$10$};
\coordinate (ra1) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (ra2) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(C)$);
\draw (ra1)--($(ra1)+(ra2)-(B)$)--(ra2);
\pic[draw,"$45^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.7cm,angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=A--C--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the exact value of $x$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\coordinate (A) at (0,3.464);
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,left] {$6$};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,below] {$x$};
\draw (C)--(A);
\coordinate (ra1) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (ra2) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(C)$);
\draw (ra1)--($(ra1)+(ra2)-(B)$)--(ra2);
\pic[draw,"$30^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.62cm,angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle=B--A--C};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The side of length $6$ is adjacent to the $30^{\circ}$ angle. Find the exact value of $x$, leaving your answer in the form $\dfrac{a}{\sqrt{3}}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.9]
\coordinate (L) at (0,0);
\coordinate (R) at (4,0);
\coordinate (T) at (2,3.464);
\coordinate (M) at (2,0);
\draw (L)--(R) node[midway,below] {$6$};
\draw (R)--(T) node[midway,above right] {$6$};
\draw (T)--(L) node[midway,above left] {$6$};
\draw[dashed] (T)--(M) node[midway,right] {$x$};
\coordinate (ra1) at ($(M)!0.3cm!(T)$);
\coordinate (ra2) at ($(M)!0.3cm!(R)$);
\draw (ra1)--($(ra1)+(ra2)-(M)$)--(ra2);
\pic[draw,"$60^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.7cm,angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=R--L--T};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The triangle is equilateral with side $6$, and $x$ is its height. Find the exact value of $x$.
